name: blip
version: '@VERSION@'
summary: A Lisp dialect with real tail calls
description: |
  blip is a Lisp dialect implemented in V, with real tail calls,
  pattern matching, and errors as values. The interpreter, standard
  library, example programs, and readme ship in the snap; run
  `blip run prog.blip`, check `blip test`, or start the REPL with a
  bare `blip`.
grade: stable
title: blip
license: MIT
contact: https://github.com/metif12/blip/issues
website: https://github.com/metif12/blip
source-code: https://github.com/metif12/blip
issues: https://github.com/metif12/blip/issues
confinement: classic
base: core24

apps:
  blip:
    command: usr/bin/blip

parts:
  blip:
    plugin: dump
    source: .
